    <!-- 9. Built for the people who debug machines (docs/24, docs/26) -->
    <section class="wrap">
      <h2>Built for the people who debug machines</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card"><span class="ic"><FjIcon name="graph" /></span><h3>See the media plane</h3><p>The live pipeline graph, with rates and drops, on the machine and in your dashboard — readable by a support engineer or an AI coding agent. <a href="/24-pipeline-introspection/">Introspection</a></p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="ic"><FjIcon name="check" /></span><h3>One command says if it's healthy</h3><p><code>sudo fjarr-agent --check</code> lists every configured source and backend, and gives the one-line fix for anything missing. <a href="/26-robot-install-and-drivers/">Install &amp; drivers</a></p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="ic"><FjIcon name="puzzle" /></span><h3>Only the drivers it needs</h3><p><code>fjarr-agent drivers detect</code> matches the hardware actually attached against a catalog and names the package each needs. Install those, and nothing else lands on the machine.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 10. Open core, honest split (docs/03, ADR-0011) -->
    <section class="wrap">
      <h2>Open core, honest split</h2>
      <table class="tiers">
        <tr><td><b>Free &amp; open</b></td><td>All three libraries, the signaling sidecar, the network link and its client, the protocol, the docs, the demos. Genuinely usable alone, self-hosted forever.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Fjarr Cloud</b></td><td>Managed signaling and relays, fleet observability, staged OTA campaigns, SSO — metered by machines, session-minutes and relay bandwidth. Same contract as self-hosting: switch either way, no rework.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><b>Licence</b></td><td>AGPL-3.0, or a commercial licence when AGPL doesn't fit your product. Nothing we ship depends on GPL code, and the build environment refuses it.</td></tr>
      </table>
      <p class="note">The whole business plan is a public document: <a href="/03-product-strategy/">product strategy</a>.</p>
    </section>

